{{Quote|My empire is forever! My empire cannot end!|Queen Karina|<ref name="Darth Vader 4" />}}
'''Karina''', known as "'''Karina the Great'''," was a [[Geonosian]] [[queen]]. The last of her kind, she was born during the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], and the [[egg]] from which she [[Reproduction|hatched]] survived the Empire's [[Sterilization of Geonosis|genocide]] on [[Geonosis]]. Prior to her birth, her egg was protected by a Geonosian known as [[Klik-Klak]], who kept it safe from both the Empire and the [[Partisans|rebel]] extremist [[Saw Gerrera]]. Klik-Klak hoped Karina would be able to repopulate the Geonosian [[species]], but she was sterile and instead attached a mechanical [[womb]] to her body. From that womb, she produced modified [[B1-series battle droid]]s with Geonosian features known as [[droid worker]]s, which she regarded as children and the future of her [[planet]].

During the [[Galactic Civil War]], Karina's existence was discovered by the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], who [[Secret mission to Geonosis|traveled]] to Geonosis to steal her [[battle droid]] [[factory]] and use it to build an [[army]] to regain the power and prestige he lost after being blamed for the destruction of the Empire's [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[battle station]] during the [[Battle of Yavin]]. Karina attempted to thwart Vader's plot with her army of [[droid]]s, but the [[Sith]] Lord and his companions&mdash;rogue [[archaeologist]] [[Chelli Lona Aphra]] and the [[assassin]] droids [[BT-1]] and [[0-0-0]]&mdash;severed and stole her mechanical womb to build battle droids of his own.

==Biography==
===Last of her kind===
{{Quote|If that egg is the last chance to save his people, then we have to help him protect it.|Ezra Bridger|<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" />}}
[[File:Klik_Klak_Geonosis_nest_Saw_Gerrera.jpg|thumb|left|300px|Klik-Klak protects the last known Geonosian queen egg from Saw Gerrera.]]
During the [[Imperial Era]], the [[Galactic Empire]] moved construction of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[superweapon]] away from [[Geonosis]], where it had been under construction by [[Geonosian]] weapons builders.<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> To protect the secret of the Death Star, the Empire [[Sterilization of Geonosis|wiped out]] the Geonosian people using [[poison gas]]<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" /> and left the planet a barren wasteland.<ref name="The Honorable Ones">{{Rebels|The Honorable Ones}}</ref> Only one Geonosian,<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|klik-klak|Klik-Klak}}</ref> he held in his possession the last known [[egg]] containing a Geonosian [[queen]]. Klik-Klak knew that the safe hatching of this egg was the only way to [[Reproduction|repopulate]] Geonosis, so he fiercely protected it in the hopes of giving his people another chance at life. Klik-Klak felt forced to defend the egg when resistance fighter [[Saw Gerrera]] led a team of [[Partisans|rebels]] to [[Mission to investigate Geonosis|investigate]] intelligence reports pointing to suspicious Imperial activity on the planet&mdash;which, though unknown to the fledgling [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]], was the remnants of the [[Project Stardust|Death Star project]]. Gerrera's team investigated an energy reading near where Klik-Klak was hiding the egg, so he ambushed the rebels and killed everyone but Gerrera.<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" />

Another rebel team, the [[Spectres]], traveled Geonosis to look for Gerrera and his [[soldier]]s, and they encountered Klik-Klak while investigating the energy readings on the planet. They discovered that Klik-Klak was protecting the egg, which Gerrera&mdash;known in the wider rebellion for his extremist tactics&mdash;threatened to destroy if Klik-Klak refused to reveal all he knew about the Empire's activities on Geonosis. The Spectres, particularly the young [[Jedi]] [[Ezra Bridger]], convinced Gerrera to back down. After helping the rebels discover the poison gas that was used to wipe out the planet's population, Klik-Klak retreated deeper beneath the planet's surface where, one day, he hoped the egg would hatch safely.<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" /> The egg ultimately did hatch,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> and the [[queen]] who was born from it took on the name Karina.<ref name="Galactic Atlas" />

===Encounter with Darth Vader===
{{Quote|Interesting tweaks on the standard droid design, too. I suspect she doesn't see these as droids. I suppose that it does make sense. Immortal queens, sterilized. The urge to continue the species by any means necessary. When biology fails, she turns to science. They aren't droids to her. They're children.|Chelli Lona Aphra|<ref name="Darth Vader 4" />}}
Klik-Klak's hopes of repopulating his [[species]] were ultimately dashed. Karina, who took shelter in a [[Cave|subterranean]] [[Karina's lair|lair]], lost her biological [[womb]] and was left sterile. Unable to repopulate her species, Karina replaced her womb with a [[portable droid factory]] acting as a mechanical womb&mdash;biology had failed her, so she turned to science to repopulate her species by any means necessary. Rather than Geonosians, she produced many [[B1-series battle droid|B1]] [[droid worker]]s, altered to look like her people. She considered the [[droid]]s her children and was fiercely protective of them, seeing them as a means to rebuild an [[Karina's empire|empire]] on Geonosis.<ref name="Darth Vader 4" /> The [[Droid Gotra]] discovered her existence and took a keen interest in her and her droid children.<ref name="Darth Vader 3">[[Darth Vader (2015) 3|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 3]]</ref>

[[File:SecretMissionGeonosianQueen-2015DarthVader4.png|thumb|right|300px|Darth Vader traveled to Geonosis to steal the droid factory from Karina.]]
After the [[Battle of Yavin]] and the destruction of the Death Star, the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] sought to build a new base of power after being blamed for the loss of the Death Star.<ref name="Darth Vader 1">[[Darth Vader (2015) 1|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 1]]</ref> After learning of Karina's droid [[factory]], Vader [[Secret mission to Geonosis|traveled]] to Geonosis with the rogue [[Archaeology|archaeologist]] [[Doctor]] [[Chelli Lona Aphra]] and her [[assassin]] droids, [[BT-1]] and [[0-0-0]].<ref name="Darth Vader 3" /> Once they arrived, they made their way into the Geonosian catacombs, where Karina's droid children tried and failed to stop them from proceeding to her lair. Vader found Karina and used his [[Darth Vader's lightsaber|lightsaber]] to sever the droid factory from her body. Injured but alive, Karina unleashed her battle droids against the Sith Lord, refusing to allow the future of her reign and all of Geonosis to be taken by an Empire that had already stolen so much from them. Vader and his companions dispatched the droids and escaped on [[Naboo Royal Starship|Vader's starship]] with the droid factory in tow. Karina survived the encounter, all while proclaiming that her empire would not end.<ref name="Darth Vader 4" />

By the [[New Republic Era]], it was believed there were no survivors on Geonosis.<ref name="Rise and Fall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref>

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|Stop them! They've ruined our past. They can't destroy our future!|Karina to her battle droid children, when Darth Vader attacked them|<ref name="Darth Vader 4" />}}
[[File:KarinaWantsBabiesBack-2015DarthVader4.png|thumb|left|250px|Karina distraught after Darth Vader stole her mechanical womb.]]
Karina was a Geonosian [[Gender|female]] with [[Color|black]] [[eye]]s and gray and tan skin.<ref name="Darth Vader 4" /> She was the last known Geonosian queen. Her successful hatching from an egg<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" /> some time prior to the Battle of Yavin<ref name="Darth Vader 4" /> signified the potential to repopulate the Geonosian species after it was wiped out by the Galactic Empire.<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" /> That potential was dashed, as Karina was sterile and could not produce offspring by the time Darth Vader encountered her. Instead, she was fitted with a mechanical womb so she could produce battle droid offspring. She was fiercely protective of these droids and considered them her children, her one and only way of restoring an empire on Geonosis. Doctor Aphra remarked that, when biology failed, Karina turned to science to ensure that Geonosis could live on.<ref name="Darth Vader 4" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|The queen egg? Is it the same queen from the Vader comic? Yeah, that is the idea. I don't want to connect too many dots 'cause that might be a story yet to be told somewhere, but the thought is that that is indeed the queen that hatches from Klik-Klak's egg.|Pablo Hidalgo, in the Warhead episode of Rebels Recon|<ref name="Rebels Recon">{{RebelsRecon|EfCuHRbbTZk|#3.14: Inside "Warhead" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-warhead}}</ref>}}
Karina was introduced in the [[Star Wars comic books|comic book]] [[Darth Vader (2015) 4|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 4]]. The comic was released on [[April 8]], [[2015]] and was written by [[Kieron Gillen]], with art by [[Salvador Larroca]].<ref name="Darth Vader 4" />

This particular Karina's backstory was revealed in "[[Ghosts of Geonosis]],"<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" /> the [[January 7]], [[2017]]<ref name="Airdate">{{TVcom|url=shows/star-wars-rebels/ghosts-of-genosis-part-one-3439510|text=Star Wars Rebels - Season 3, Episode 12: Ghosts of Genosis, Part One}}</ref> episode of the [[Star Wars Rebels Season Three|third season]] of the animated television series ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]''. Though the character herself does not appear, the egg that she later hatches from is a vital part of the episode, as is the idea of preserving the Geonosian race after the Empire carried out its genocide on the planet.<ref name="Ghosts of Geonosis" /> Hidalgo later revealed in the "[[Rebels Recon]]" episode for "[[Warhead (episode)|Warhead]]" that the idea was that the egg did indeed contain Karina.<ref name="Rebels Recon" />

